  "report_references": [
    {
      "evidence": "We need to check the command arity in IO threads, if it is not correct, we should reset it, as we may do memory prefetching according to the `iolookedcmd`.  Accessing `argv` using the key positions returned by `getKeysFromCommand` is unsafe and must be avoided for invalid commands. Otherwise, this may lead to invalid memory access and potentially cause the redis to crash.\r\n\r\nThis bug starts to have an impact after #14017",
